WEBVTT

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:03.680
That's enough!

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:09.140
Your coordination still has some weak spots,
 but you've gotten pretty good.

00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:11.910
Huh? Is she actually praising us?

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:14.000
She most certainly is.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:16.340
Praise from Takako is rare.

00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:17.150
Yay!

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:18.830
Don't get cocky.

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:21.530
You still haven't managed to get a point yet.

00:00:21.530 --> 00:00:22.930
Yes, ma'am.

00:00:22.930 --> 00:00:25.440
Ah, bath time.

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:48.470
<b>Katana Maidens</b>

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:06.390
<b>Episode 9  After the Festival</b>

00:02:09.630 --> 00:02:14.180
Gosh, your back is so 
small and adorable, Saaya.

00:02:14.180 --> 00:02:17.700
I don't know whether it's that 
I feel I can't leave you alone,

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:21.330
or that I feel I need to protect you,
 but you just set off my maternal instincts.

00:02:22.490 --> 00:02:23.850
What the heck?

00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:29.550
Individual fights are fun and all, 
but team fighting is fun, too!

00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:32.850
We still don't have a lot of
actual battle experience,

00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:37.140
so having things like an attack 
squad and a mobile squad is new.

00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:37.970
Yeah.

00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:40.880
You're so strong, Kanami-chan.

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:42.340
So are you, Mai-chan!

00:02:43.150 --> 00:02:45.070
When we were facing off against Satomi-san,

00:02:45.070 --> 00:02:49.110
you attacked at the same time as Kaoru-chan,
and hesitated for a moment, didn't you?

00:02:49.110 --> 00:02:52.130
If you had attacked like that I'm 
sure we would've gotten a point.

00:02:52.910 --> 00:02:54.890
So you saw that much.

00:02:54.890 --> 00:02:59.110
I'm not sure if it's that I saw it,
 or was able to see it...

00:02:59.110 --> 00:03:01.500
You really are strong, Kanami-chan.

00:03:02.290 --> 00:03:06.470
Even after hearing that story about
 your mother, you're still trying to fight.

00:03:06.470 --> 00:03:11.360
No, I guess it's because you heard 
the story about your mother,

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:13.350
but for me...

00:03:13.350 --> 00:03:15.660
You have no reason to fight, do you?

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:18.660
If you don't have a reason, 
then you don't need to fight.

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:19.920
Just stay here.

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:23.550
I'm sure Mokusa will harbor 
you until things settle down.

00:03:23.950 --> 00:03:27.300
But you and Kanami-chan are going, right?

00:03:27.910 --> 00:03:29.680
Because we have a connection.

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:35.930
Those two will also likely face 
battle because they're with Mokusa.

00:03:35.930 --> 00:03:39.380
But you and Itomi do not 
need to come with us.

00:03:39.380 --> 00:03:41.680
I will destroy Origami Yukari.

00:03:46.860 --> 00:03:48.450
Mai-chan...

00:03:53.910 --> 00:03:56.340
It's pretty noisy outside.

00:03:56.340 --> 00:04:00.180
Of course it is. After all,
 today is the festival.

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:01.380
Festival?

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:04.090
This village has one twice a year, apparently.

00:04:05.450 --> 00:04:06.770
Did you hear that, Mai-chan?

00:04:06.770 --> 00:04:09.970
Practice is over and everything, 
so let's go check it out later.

00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:11.520
Okay, sure.

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:13.820
A festival! This is so exciting!

00:04:14.430 --> 00:04:15.350
Huh?

00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:17.920
My uniform is gone.

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:19.350
So is mine.

00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:21.120
Don't tell me...

00:04:25.460 --> 00:04:28.850
If you're looking for your uniforms, 
they've been sent to the cleaners.

00:04:29.530 --> 00:04:32.030
They'll be ready later tonight.

00:04:32.030 --> 00:04:34.660
In the meantime, here you go.

00:04:34.660 --> 00:04:38.310
Wow! Yukata! So refined.

00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:41.220
Professor Friedman prepared them for you.

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:44.010
He said you should wear these,
 and go enjoy the festival.

00:04:45.630 --> 00:04:47.440
That's my grandpa for you!

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:49.760
He's so understanding.

00:04:54.180 --> 00:04:56.890
Wow, it's the perfect size.

00:04:56.890 --> 00:04:59.490
How did that old man figure that out?

00:04:59.490 --> 00:05:01.560
That's my grandpa for you.

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:04.370
Come on, put yours on too, Hiyori-chan.

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:06.430
This isn't the time for such frivolity.

00:05:06.430 --> 00:05:07.620
It's a festival!

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:10.070
If we can't celebrate today, 
then when will we ever get to?

00:05:10.070 --> 00:05:11.620
Come on, put it on.

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:13.070
H-Hey...

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:19.310
It looks good on you, Hiyori-chan.

00:05:24.830 --> 00:05:27.540
Aren't we going to the festival?

00:05:28.440 --> 00:05:30.540
Yeah! Let's go guys!

00:06:01.420 --> 00:06:03.290
What series is that from?

00:06:10.810 --> 00:06:13.040
Ellen, it's about time.

00:06:13.040 --> 00:06:14.250
You're right.

00:06:16.550 --> 00:06:21.870
There's something we want you all to see.

00:06:22.740 --> 00:06:24.170
What's that?

00:06:24.170 --> 00:06:29.050
My grandpa wishes to invite you to 
the main event for today's festival.

00:06:29.530 --> 00:06:31.280
Main event?

00:06:33.590 --> 00:06:34.770
It's so beautiful.

00:06:35.290 --> 00:06:38.510
I found you, Hiyori-chan and Kanami-chan!

00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:40.940
Rui-san?!

00:06:41.410 --> 00:06:43.470
How are you two doing?

00:06:43.470 --> 00:06:46.370
What about you? Were you all right 
after everything that happened?

00:06:46.370 --> 00:06:48.590
Of course she wasn't.

00:06:48.590 --> 00:06:51.410
Ruippe was apparently arrested,

00:06:51.410 --> 00:06:54.590
as a suspect in the assault 
on Origami Yukari.

00:06:55.130 --> 00:06:58.140
So then that was because we intruded on you.

00:06:58.140 --> 00:07:00.150
Don't worry about it.

00:07:00.150 --> 00:07:04.050
President Hashima pulled some strings, 
and I was released immediately.

00:07:04.050 --> 00:07:06.110
So that's what happened.

00:07:06.110 --> 00:07:07.600
You're Mai-chan, aren't you?

00:07:07.600 --> 00:07:09.860
And Sayaka-chan, it's been a while.

00:07:09.860 --> 00:07:12.470
Do you know her too, Sayaka-chan?

00:07:12.470 --> 00:07:14.770
I attacked her home.

00:07:14.770 --> 00:07:15.570
Huh?!

00:07:15.570 --> 00:07:17.750
Now, let's go then, shall we?

00:07:17.750 --> 00:07:21.830
You've been invited, right? 
All of you, by FineMan.

00:07:30.710 --> 00:07:33.210
It's Takako-san and Satomi-san!

00:07:38.440 --> 00:07:40.480
That's a shintai?

00:07:41.220 --> 00:07:43.290
I wonder what's in it?

00:07:43.720 --> 00:07:45.140
It's noro.

00:07:46.420 --> 00:07:50.350
There's still noro that the 
Origami family hasn't collected?

00:07:50.350 --> 00:07:51.680
Surprised?

00:07:51.680 --> 00:07:55.220
There aren't as many as there 
used to be, but there are still

00:07:55.220 --> 00:07:57.740
shrines in this country that 
worship noro like this.

00:07:57.740 --> 00:07:59.220
Worship?

00:07:59.220 --> 00:08:02.620
Yes, they worship it 
politely and respectfully.

00:08:02.620 --> 00:08:07.620
Do you know how noro was created 
to begin with, Kanami-kun?

00:08:07.620 --> 00:08:09.060
Um....

00:08:09.060 --> 00:08:12.900
While refining the tamahagane steel
 used to forge okatana,

00:08:12.900 --> 00:08:15.000
noro is separated out as an impurity.

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:16.950
You're very good, Mai-kun.

00:08:16.950 --> 00:08:19.300
Noro that is separated from 
tamahagane steel,

00:08:19.300 --> 00:08:22.020
which has the power to become an okatana,

00:08:22.020 --> 00:08:25.260
has almost the same divinity 
as the okatana itself.

00:08:25.260 --> 00:08:29.520
Even with the technology we 
have today, we cannot erase it.

00:08:29.520 --> 00:08:32.150
But we were told that if it's left alone,

00:08:32.150 --> 00:08:35.650
it'll turn into an aradama, and that's 
why the Origami family manages it.

00:08:35.650 --> 00:08:37.630
And that is incorrect.

00:08:37.630 --> 00:08:38.650
Huh?

00:08:39.430 --> 00:08:41.910
Let's try continuing this somewhere else.

00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:48.410
Noro was once worshiped in shrines
 like this all over the country.

00:08:48.410 --> 00:08:52.110
We started managing the 
collection of it as we do now

00:08:52.110 --> 00:08:54.170
around the end of the Meiji period.

00:08:54.170 --> 00:08:56.750
The government at the time 
wanted to reduce the number

00:08:56.750 --> 00:09:01.550
of shrines primarily for economic reasons, 
and so they were consolidated together.

00:09:01.830 --> 00:09:06.750
Naturally, as a result, the noro was turned 
into spectrum meters or became aradama.

00:09:06.750 --> 00:09:09.330
In order to prevent that,
 the Origami family at the time

00:09:09.330 --> 00:09:12.060
strictly managed the amount of noro.

00:09:12.060 --> 00:09:15.700
However, as the signs of an 
oncoming war intensified,

00:09:15.700 --> 00:09:19.940
voices calling for military
 use of noro increased,

00:09:19.940 --> 00:09:22.070
and the restrictions were removed.

00:09:22.490 --> 00:09:24.070
For military use?

00:09:24.070 --> 00:09:25.890
They sought to amplify the 
divinity of the noro...

00:09:25.890 --> 00:09:29.300
In short, its power to interfere with 
the netherworld that, until then,

00:09:29.300 --> 00:09:35.830
had only been expressly permitted 
for you Toji to use in battle.

00:09:35.830 --> 00:09:38.610
After the war, the collection 
of noro was accelerated

00:09:38.610 --> 00:09:40.510
as the United States Army joined the study.

00:09:40.920 --> 00:09:43.990
Officially, they said that it was safer 
to gather the dangerous noro in one place

00:09:43.990 --> 00:09:47.120
and manage it that way 
rather than dispersing it,

00:09:47.120 --> 00:09:49.770
and they began gathering 
noro all across Japan.

00:09:49.770 --> 00:09:52.830
But there were unforeseen consequences.

00:09:52.830 --> 00:09:56.560
The more noro from spectrum meters
 that was gathered together,

00:09:56.560 --> 00:09:59.020
the more it acquired intelligence.

00:09:59.020 --> 00:10:01.600
Then does that mean if 
you gather lots of noro,

00:10:01.600 --> 00:10:04.450
you can create an intelligent aradama?

00:10:06.280 --> 00:10:08.780
To put it simply, that is what happens.

00:10:09.140 --> 00:10:10.930
Currently, the Origami family

00:10:10.930 --> 00:10:15.090
has stockpiled a vast amount of noro,
more than has ever been in one place before.

00:10:15.090 --> 00:10:16.000
That's...

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:18.980
Why you believe Princess Tagitsu is god-like...

00:10:18.980 --> 00:10:21.170
That's not the only problem.

00:10:21.170 --> 00:10:25.350
If that massive amount of noro is stimulated 
by something and becomes an aradama—

00:10:25.350 --> 00:10:30.930
no, a great aradama, there is 
no way we could control it.

00:10:31.250 --> 00:10:35.440
Much like what happened in the 
Great Disaster of Sagami Bay.

00:10:35.440 --> 00:10:37.310
What do you mean?

00:10:37.310 --> 00:10:41.440
That disaster is an accident that 
happened as a result of trying

00:10:41.440 --> 00:10:45.650
to transport a fully-loaded tanker
 of noro to the United States.

00:10:46.230 --> 00:10:51.070
In other words, it was a man-made 
disaster caused by human arrogance.

00:11:00.400 --> 00:11:04.090
We should never have disturbed its sleep.

00:11:04.510 --> 00:11:07.350
Noro is a victim, so to speak,

00:11:07.350 --> 00:11:10.850
forced into existence by humans
 who wish to create okatana.

00:11:10.850 --> 00:11:14.030
If we can't go back to the 
way things used to be,

00:11:14.030 --> 00:11:17.850
we could, at the very least,
 enshrine it and let it rest peacefully.

00:11:17.850 --> 00:11:23.110
That is the only thing 
we can do to atone now.

00:11:23.110 --> 00:11:26.080
The aradama are victims?

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:28.990
Then that means everything 
we've been doing...

00:11:29.360 --> 00:11:34.990
Toji use their okatana to purify noro
 that has become an aradama.

00:11:34.990 --> 00:11:38.640
That does save people's lives. But...

00:11:39.470 --> 00:11:43.590
The first Toji are said to have been
 maidens who served in the shrines.

00:11:43.590 --> 00:11:46.720
Which means you all have to properly take on

00:11:46.720 --> 00:11:50.140
the duties of a shrine maiden,
 rather than just defeating aradama.

00:12:00.770 --> 00:12:02.900
How did they take it?

00:12:02.900 --> 00:12:05.150
They bore it, as we expected.

00:12:05.150 --> 00:12:06.400
Of course they did.

00:12:06.400 --> 00:12:11.680
Even the five schools teach a version of
 the truth warped by Origami Yukari.

00:12:11.680 --> 00:12:14.720
They won't be able to accept 
everything so easily.

00:12:14.720 --> 00:12:17.410
Especially an honor student like Mai-kun.

00:12:18.380 --> 00:12:20.790
They have to accept it.

00:12:20.790 --> 00:12:23.290
All the more because they are Toji.

00:12:23.290 --> 00:12:26.080
What will they do?

00:12:26.080 --> 00:12:27.300
I do not know.

00:12:27.980 --> 00:12:33.450
But whatever decision they make,
 I would like to respect it.

00:12:34.550 --> 00:12:38.560
That's our job as Mokusa, as well.

00:12:55.450 --> 00:12:57.450
You changed, too?

00:12:57.450 --> 00:12:59.790
The festival was a lot of fun.

00:12:59.790 --> 00:13:00.930
Yeah.

00:13:00.930 --> 00:13:03.900
I wonder if our mothers 
went to it together, too.

00:13:04.460 --> 00:13:05.960
Who knows?

00:13:10.950 --> 00:13:12.060
Kanami...

00:13:13.340 --> 00:13:14.800
Kogarasumaru?

00:13:15.900 --> 00:13:17.600
Chidori, too.

00:13:17.600 --> 00:13:20.340
Maybe it was fate.

00:13:20.340 --> 00:13:26.330
We carry the swords our mothers used,
 and we found each other.

00:13:28.980 --> 00:13:30.810
They probably went.

00:13:31.320 --> 00:13:31.950
Hm?

00:13:32.490 --> 00:13:37.490
To the festival. Your mom 
and my mom, together.

00:13:38.490 --> 00:13:40.640
Yeah, I'm sure they did.

00:13:44.410 --> 00:13:47.380
What can I do, though?

00:13:47.380 --> 00:13:49.570
You can do anything.

00:13:49.570 --> 00:13:50.510
Huh?

00:13:50.510 --> 00:13:53.880
I'm also trying to think of what I can do.

00:13:54.350 --> 00:13:55.810
Sayaka-chan...

00:13:59.510 --> 00:14:02.350
The festival will be over soon.

00:14:02.350 --> 00:14:05.390
If the noro is broken up
 and enshrined again,

00:14:05.390 --> 00:14:08.110
then there will be festivals 
like this all over Japan.

00:14:08.110 --> 00:14:11.140
When that happens, let's go play together!

00:14:11.140 --> 00:14:14.750
All together with Hiyoyon, 
Kanamin, Maimai, and Saaya.

00:14:15.390 --> 00:14:16.320
Sure.

00:14:23.630 --> 00:14:26.400
It's so shiny!

00:14:42.390 --> 00:14:47.020
So, you're going to work together with us?

00:14:47.020 --> 00:14:49.460
Yes, if by that you mean 
to correct the distortion

00:14:49.460 --> 00:14:53.530
and return the Toji to their original 
roles, then our goals are the same.

00:14:54.060 --> 00:14:57.530
I will defeat the main 
cause, Origami Yukari.

00:14:59.550 --> 00:15:04.160
I think it would be a pleasure to 
have more skilled Toji.

00:15:05.030 --> 00:15:06.420
You're so...

00:15:07.370 --> 00:15:08.720
All right.

00:15:08.720 --> 00:15:10.510
I understand how you feel.

00:15:10.510 --> 00:15:13.920
Mokusa will welcome you. However...

00:15:14.260 --> 00:15:15.380
There's trouble!

00:15:15.380 --> 00:15:17.090
What is it?

00:15:24.930 --> 00:15:27.310
This is the special military unit.

00:15:27.310 --> 00:15:31.310
This area has been designated
 a special disaster prediction zone.

00:15:31.310 --> 00:15:35.390
Please move quickly according 
to our instructions.

00:15:35.390 --> 00:15:36.070
I repeat...

00:15:36.730 --> 00:15:38.030
The Origami family?

00:15:38.820 --> 00:15:41.610
They don't seem to be hunting aradama.

00:15:42.330 --> 00:15:45.780
So we're already being treated as criminals?

00:15:45.780 --> 00:15:48.080
But how did they find out about this village?

00:15:48.080 --> 00:15:51.150
Now is not the time to investigate that.

00:15:51.150 --> 00:15:54.310
Are they trying to detain 
everyone in the village?

00:15:54.310 --> 00:15:55.300
Probably.

00:15:55.300 --> 00:15:58.560
And then they likely intend 
to screen out anyone

00:15:58.560 --> 00:16:00.720
involved with Mokusa and arrest them.

00:16:00.720 --> 00:16:02.850
Now, then, what shall we do?

00:16:02.850 --> 00:16:05.540
We cannot be captured here.

00:16:05.540 --> 00:16:08.270
Then we will carry out a strategic retreat.

00:16:08.270 --> 00:16:10.480
How are we going to retreat?

00:16:10.480 --> 00:16:15.040
It might be a bit difficult like this,
 but we will take the submarine.

00:16:15.040 --> 00:16:18.100
That ship remains affiliated with the US Navy.

00:16:18.100 --> 00:16:21.700
They are not an opponent a police 
organization like theirs can handle.

00:16:21.700 --> 00:16:23.870
Will that work, Akane-sama?

00:16:26.490 --> 00:16:27.500
It's settled.

00:16:27.850 --> 00:16:29.350
Let's split into two groups.

00:16:29.350 --> 00:16:31.620
I will take Akane-sama and 
the others to the pier.

00:16:31.620 --> 00:16:34.790
I will gather up the other Toji, 
and we'll stand our ground here.

00:16:34.790 --> 00:16:36.500
Satomi, I leave the rest to you.

00:16:36.500 --> 00:16:37.510
Right.

00:16:37.510 --> 00:16:39.620
Um, what should we do?

00:16:39.620 --> 00:16:42.510
You all come with me.
 That includes you, Ellen, and Kaoru.

00:16:46.760 --> 00:16:48.380
This is our escape route?

00:16:49.250 --> 00:16:52.870
This used to be a naval base back in the day.

00:16:52.870 --> 00:16:55.150
It has been thoroughly 
prepared for emergencies.

00:16:55.150 --> 00:16:56.620
Now, let's go!

00:17:02.410 --> 00:17:04.160
Come at us already!

00:17:05.660 --> 00:17:07.240
Sorry for the wait!

00:17:12.430 --> 00:17:13.490
You're—!

00:17:14.000 --> 00:17:18.640
I'm Tsubakuro Yume, the fourth member 
of Origami Yukari's elite guard.

00:17:18.640 --> 00:17:22.010
While I may be the fourth member,
 I am the strongest.

00:17:22.340 --> 00:17:23.220
Draw your swords!

00:17:26.510 --> 00:17:28.080
Nikkari Aoe...

00:17:35.750 --> 00:17:37.230
Such strength...

00:17:37.230 --> 00:17:40.570
You ladies are too weak.

00:17:45.490 --> 00:17:48.080
As expected, they've already secured here.

00:17:48.080 --> 00:17:50.030
Are they going to strike?

00:17:50.030 --> 00:17:51.270
Probably.

00:17:51.270 --> 00:17:52.800
I mean, take a look.

00:17:52.800 --> 00:17:56.080
They're equipped with spectrum finders.

00:17:56.080 --> 00:17:58.550
All of the members of Mokusa are human.

00:17:58.550 --> 00:18:01.970
Why would they need those
 for detecting things?

00:18:01.970 --> 00:18:03.060
Then...

00:18:03.060 --> 00:18:05.340
Please try to remember what happened at Izu.

00:18:05.680 --> 00:18:08.210
Even though you could 
see aradama before you,

00:18:08.210 --> 00:18:11.770
the spectrum finder had 
no reaction whatsoever.

00:18:11.770 --> 00:18:14.750
Does that mean the government-issued 
devices have been modified?

00:18:14.750 --> 00:18:16.510
Most likely, that is the case.

00:18:16.510 --> 00:18:18.510
Those devices are made from technology

00:18:18.510 --> 00:18:21.860
developed by the Origami family,
 just like the S Equipment.

00:18:21.860 --> 00:18:27.030
At this point, yes, it means the devices 
have been set to react to okatana.

00:18:28.280 --> 00:18:31.540
Several aradama have been detected.
 They're very close.

00:18:31.540 --> 00:18:32.450
Be careful!

00:18:33.210 --> 00:18:36.710
At this rate, we will be treated as aradama.

00:18:36.710 --> 00:18:39.670
So aradama are calling humans aradama now?

00:18:39.670 --> 00:18:40.870
Damn it, let's go!

00:18:40.870 --> 00:18:41.920
Wait.

00:18:41.920 --> 00:18:44.460
Those men are only following orders.

00:18:44.910 --> 00:18:46.210
I know.

00:18:46.930 --> 00:18:49.180
Toji have really become aradama?

00:18:49.180 --> 00:18:51.770
Fire! They aren't human, they're aradama!

00:19:01.030 --> 00:19:02.230
Don't remove your utsushi!

00:19:02.230 --> 00:19:03.280
Be careful!

00:19:04.150 --> 00:19:05.240
Hang in there!

00:19:05.240 --> 00:19:08.300
If she removes her utsushi now,
the arrow will remain behind in her body.

00:19:08.990 --> 00:19:10.240
This is going to hurt a bit.

00:19:10.240 --> 00:19:11.490
Do it!

00:19:11.490 --> 00:19:12.430
Here we go.

00:19:14.160 --> 00:19:15.490
These are...

00:19:15.490 --> 00:19:18.670
Weapons that seal a Toji's movements.

00:19:19.050 --> 00:19:22.860
Nee-sama... I can't believe you 
would use something like this.

00:19:32.650 --> 00:19:35.660
Not enough. This is not nearly enough.

00:19:38.110 --> 00:19:40.460
They're over there, huh?

00:19:44.030 --> 00:19:45.650
Akane-sama, hurry!

00:19:45.650 --> 00:19:47.030
I'm sorry.

00:19:47.030 --> 00:19:49.980
Etou! Yanase! Hurry up! Everyone get in!

00:19:55.790 --> 00:19:57.170
Mai-chan, hurry!

00:19:57.170 --> 00:19:57.910
Okay!

00:19:57.910 --> 00:19:59.170
You go first.

00:20:00.170 --> 00:20:01.800
Take care of Akane-sama!

00:20:01.800 --> 00:20:02.670
Takako-san?

00:20:02.670 --> 00:20:07.130
Man, I didn't make it? Shucks.

00:20:07.440 --> 00:20:09.630
What happened to the Toji at the shrine?

00:20:09.630 --> 00:20:11.840
Toji? Them?

00:20:11.840 --> 00:20:14.580
They weren't able to resist at all, though.

00:20:14.580 --> 00:20:18.390
But the girl who used this 
okatana was a bit better, I guess.

00:20:20.900 --> 00:20:22.400
Satomi...

00:20:22.400 --> 00:20:25.330
You're gonna fight like that?

00:20:25.330 --> 00:20:28.280
I'll wait for you, so why 
don't you take out that arrow?

00:20:28.720 --> 00:20:31.240
Or should I help you?

00:20:31.240 --> 00:20:32.800
Not necessary.

00:20:34.870 --> 00:20:38.120
I won't lose to Toji who rely on aradama!

00:20:39.130 --> 00:20:40.250
Is that so?

00:20:49.340 --> 00:20:54.100
I've never used even a 
bit of aradama to fight.

00:20:54.390 --> 00:20:57.340
This is entirely my own ability!

00:21:04.310 --> 00:21:07.360
I wonder how Yume is doing now?

00:21:07.360 --> 00:21:11.610
That girl doesn't know the 
meaning of the word "restraint."

00:23:34.840 --> 00:23:39.840
<b>Next Episode  Resolve for Tomorrow</b>
